# The registry is a generated artifact that consumers byte-copy: `spec install`
# uses copyFile, so whatever is in THIS working tree lands verbatim in every
# consumer's .spec-packages cache.
#
# This repo runs core.autocrlf=true, so without this file checkout rewrote every
# component to CRLF even though the object store holds LF - and the CRLF then
# propagated outward. In Vector that surfaced as ~25 files reported modified
# with an EMPTY diff after every `spec install`, unfixable from that end: the
# published set was a MIX, so declaring either ending there left the other
# subset mismatched (measured: 25 files one way, 63 the other).
#
# Pin the working tree to LF so the bytes on disk match the bytes in the object
# store, and so a consumer can declare `eol=lf` and have it hold. `text=auto`
# still lets git detect and skip anything binary.
#
# Paired with the publish-side fix in spec's packages/cli/src/lib/reconcile.ts,
# which normalizes on the spec-to-registry write so CRLF cannot re-enter here.
* text=auto eol=lf
